{"question_id": "V2-dev-RPT-en-T2-002", "approach": "HYBRID+intact", "approach_base": "HYBRID", "flags": {"intact": true}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "D", "corpus_set": "D_en", "answer_text": "Delivery Hero treats the pre-August 2021 Spanish model as probable and provisions for it, while the post-August 2021 model is treated as only possible and disclosed as a contingency.\n\n- For the model operated by Glovo until August 2021, the risk is more likely than not to materialize, so appropriate provisions are reflected in the Consolidated Financial Statements (Strategic Risks, [4]).\n- During 2024, Glovo had to provide Spanish courts with bank guarantees to secure payment of the liabilities claimed by the authorities for that earlier operational model (Strategic Risks, [1], [3]).\n- For the model in place since August 2021, the rider risk is deemed possible but not probable, so it is disclosed as a contingency — a contingent liability of €440 to 770 million for the ongoing social security investigation (Strategic Risks [4]; Auditor's Report [2]; Contingencies [5]).\n- No provision has been recognized for the post-August 2021 model because reclassification by Spanish courts was assessed as not probable (Contingencies, [5]).\n- Glovo's management decided to progressively move to an employment-based model in Spain to avoid further legal uncertainties regarding the model in place since August 2021 (Strategic Risks, [1]).\n- Nevertheless, in relation to the ongoing investigations, Glovo will defend the self-employed status through all available instances and continue cooperating with the Spanish authorities (Strategic Risks, [1]).", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 1013 chars]", "doc_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en", "section_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::h201", "unit_ids": ["D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::p127_b42", "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::p128_b5", "D.deliveryhero_